646|cubeloop|CubeLoop has a shipped async, externally bound model/tool execution path with streamed observations and new tool choices, checkpointed sessions, optional ephemeral subagents and goal-feedback continuation (S1=A). Its concurrent tools, child-task dispatch, session queue and deferred tools serve one caller goal rather than dampening interference among independently viable S1 departments (S2=—). Caller-defined HITL approval, run control, TODO guards and checkpointing do not supply a discretionary whole-current managerial owner over such departments (S3=—). The optional independent goal-evaluator model scores current-goal attainment from recent transcript and feeds the same worker; tracing/receipts lack independent inspection of operating reality with a corrective management return (S3*=—). Configured model fallback, current-task goal retries and TODO revisions do not select and adopt prospective organizational strategy for future runs (S4=—); host task/config authority and per-call human approvals are not a first-party ultimate-identity or constitutional policy authority (S5=—). Review is pinned and source-only, not a claim of external provider execution quality.
