650|matterloop|MatterLoop is an embeddable Python SDK for bounded, stateful, model-backed AgentLoop and TeamOrchestrator goal execution, including dynamic plans, delegated agent tasks, tool results and verifier feedback (S1=A). Capability-aware least-load worker selection, DAG coordination and checkpoint/CAS are deterministic components of one submitted task/team rather than inter-S1 disturbance damping between separately viable operating businesses (S2=—). Model TeamReviewer can inspect the whole current draft, accept, replan, pause or stop, but this manages one finite deliverable rather than a standing independently accountable current controller of several viable operating departments (S3=—). Independent task verification and event/tool audit check work-product claims, not the reality of an S3 management report through complementary autonomous organizational audit and returned correction (S3*=—). StrategyOptimizer suggests prompt/tool/plan adjustments, memory reuse and LoopEngineeringRuntime can improve a subsequent attempt within the same goal; no autonomous outside-and-then strategic environmental selection and accepted future organizational capability change is established (S4=—). Host-supplied tool access limits, approval and resource policy do not provide a legitimate internal or parent-governed identity/constitutional authority returning ultimate-policy decisions (S5=—). Classification is first-party source-bounded, not proof of paid model performance or deployment-specific institutional governance.
