697|codeaf|CodeAF's standard worker graph drives model-chosen tool actions and repair from task feedback (S1=A). Model-based dependency binding and finishability counter-audit alter required predecessor inputs between separate worker leaves, regulating inter-task interference rather than merely dispatching a queue (S2=A). Its model head reads the whole installed resident's active board and issues current task/cancel/change commands, while a separate attended human-owner control mode also returns portfolio interventions (S3=A(P)); dependency/delivery audits do not independently audit S3 management judgments (S3*=—). Model-led distillation of prior task outcomes can persist scoped notebook lessons or validated craft workflows and feed later tasks, supporting bounded prospective adaptation despite explicitly documented open secondary learning circuits (S4=A). Only the local user can ratify and expand standing purposes and permissions, with future ambient actions consuming that authority (S5=P).
