726|picode|picode's shipped single model-driven coding loop chooses workspace file, shell and finish actions from tool feedback (S1=A). Serial tool batches, a busy-task guard and resumable sessions do not coordinate multiple independently acting S1 cells (S2=—), and one-task human abort/command approval is not whole-current supervisory management (S3=—). Self-invoked checks and scripted development tests are not complementary independent operational audit (S3*=—). Optional model summaries of prior conversation and user-set provider configuration are not prospective adaptive intelligence (S4=—), while workspace policies, shell approval and static prompt constraints do not decide ultimate identity policy (S5=—).
727|whipcode|WhipCode's retained recursive model-driven coding agents act independently (S1=A); parent-selected division of parallel work and versioned shared-state conflict feedback regulate inter-child interference (S2=A). Its model-facing child portfolio and steering/stop decisions close current control, with a separate operator tree-inspection and intervention mode (S3=A(P)). Generic reviewer examples and product evaluations are not a shipped complementary operational audit (S3*=—); task memory, schedules and MCP/skill imports are not prospective capability strategy (S4=—), nor are permission grants and prompt rules ultimate identity governance (S5=—).
728|microcodex|MicroCodex's one model-driven C++23 coding loop chooses five file, glob and bash tools and revises work from their results (S1=A). Parallel function-call futures remain actions of that same S1, not coordination among independent work cells (S2=—); interruption, retry and saved conversation control do not oversee a whole current agent portfolio (S3=—). Repository black-box tests are not an installed complementary operational auditor (S3*=—). Local Codex skill discovery and task-context compaction do not close prospective capability adaptation (S4=—), while a lexical bash denylist and prompt instructions do not decide ultimate identity policy (S5=—).
